CT    Interspersed_Repeat;Transposable_Element;Class_I_Retrotransposition;LINE-dependent_Retroposon;SINE;tRNA_Promoter;V-core;RTE-end
MS    TaxId:7954 TaxName:Danio
CC    Ps 1-64 are tRNA-derived (Pol III promoter A box at pos 11-22, B-box at
CC    55-64), (TG)n at 232-250, poly-At tail from 368-373. DANA was the first
CC    SINE isolated from zebrafish (Danio rerio) exhibiting all the hallmarks
CC    of these tRNA-derived elements. DANA is unique in its clearly defined
CC    substructure of distinct cassettes. In contrast to generic SINE
CC    elements, DANA appears to have been assembled by insertions of short
CC    sequences into a progenitor, tRNA-derived element. Once associated with
CC    each other, these subunits were amplified as a new transposable element
CC    with such a remarkable success that DANA-related sequences comprise
CC    approximately 10% of the modern zebrafish genome. At least some of the
CC    sequences comprised by the full-length element were capable of movement,
CC    forming a new group of mobile, composite transposons, one of which
CC    caused an insertional mutation in the zebrafish no tail gene. Being
CC    present only in the genus Danio, and estimated to be as old as the genus
CC    itself, DANA may have played a role in Danio speciation by massive
CC    amplification and genome-wide dispersion. There are extensive DNA
CC    polymorphisms between zebrafish populations and strains detected by PCR
CC    amplification using primers specific to DANA, suggesting that the DANA
CC    element will be useful as a molecular tool for genetic and phylogenetic
CC    analyses.
